    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "BUILD SUCCESS \u2014 the full test suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe `householdId` is now deterministic and drives all household-keyed behaviour. Changes (kept as small, cohesive units to minimize structural impact):\n\n1. **New `HouseholdId` helper** (`rest/function/owner/HouseholdId.java`) \u2014 a single-method utility, mirroring the existing `IdentityKey`/`PossibleDuplicate` pattern, that computes the first 12 upper-case hex chars of `SHA-256(normalizedLastName + '|' + postcode)`. Owners with the same last name + postcode get the same id automatically, with no stored link.\n\n2. **`EnsureUniqueOwnerHousehold`** \u2014 rewritten to assign `HouseholdId.of(owner)` and reject (409) any owner whose computed `householdId` matches an existing owner's, *unless* `sharesHousehold=true`, which now only bypasses that block (the id is assigned either way). Its private hashing helpers were removed into the new class, leaving it a single simple method.\n\n3. **`owners.POST.yml`** \u2014 wired the `ensureUniqueHousehold` step in before `ensureUniqueIdentity`, so `householdId` is set before the identity check, the household-size count (`AssignOwnerHouseholdSize`, already keyed on `householdId`), and the responder all read it.\n\n4. **`RespondWithOwnerCreated`** \u2014 a declared household member (`sharesHousehold=true`) is no longer flagged as a possible duplicate.\n\nNet effect: same last name + postcode \u21d2 same `householdId`; a second such owner is a 409 household duplicate unless it declares `sharesHousehold`, in which case it's created as a member and not flagged as a suspected duplicate \u2014 exactly the specified behaviour. The acceptance test `coreSameLastNameAndPostcodeShareHouseholdId` and the full suite pass.",
